  "nl_text": "The rschema_0158 database is designed to manage a system for creating and administering exams. The database contains seven tables, each representing a distinct entity within the system. The Role table stores information about different roles within the system, with a unique Role ID and a corresponding role name. The Category table holds details about different categories of questions, identified by a unique category ID and category name. The User table stores information about individual users, including their contact information, name, and role ID, which links them to a specific role in the system. The Question table contains details about individual questions, such as their category ID, content, correct answer, difficulty level, explanation, and options, with a unique question ID. The Exam table stores information about exams, including their creator ID, description, exam name, status, time range, and a unique exam ID. The Exam_Question table links exams to specific questions, with a unique combination of exam and question IDs, and a sequence number for the question within the exam. The User_Answer_Sheet table tracks user answers to exams, including the exam ID, score, student ID, and submission time, with a unique combination of student and exam IDs. Each table has constraints to ensure data integrity, such as primary keys to uniquely identify each record, foreign keys to link related records, and not null constraints to prevent missing values in required fields. For example, a user must be assigned a role, and an exam must have a creator. Additionally, the database includes indexes and constraints to optimize data retrieval and prevent data inconsistencies, such as the composite primary key in the Exam_Question table and the unique constraints on the primary keys of each table.",
  "gold_question": "The online examination system shall include functions such as user management, question bank management, and exam management.\nThe system shall have different user roles, such as student, teacher, and administrator. Each user shall have a unique ID, real name, contact information, and other details.\nThe question bank shall contain various questions. Each question shall have a difficulty level, content, options, correct answer, explanation, and belong to a category.\nAdministrators shall be able to create exams, set the exam name, description, time range, status, and select questions from the question bank to include in the exam, specifying the order of the questions.\nStudents shall be able to take exams. After submitting answers, the system shall record the exam score and the answer status for each question, including the user's answer and whether it is correct.\nThe exam score shall include the student's score and submission time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0158.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0158\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`category_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`role_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `question` (\n  `question_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `correct_answer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `difficulty_level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `explanation` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `options` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`question_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `question_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`category_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `exam` (\n  `exam_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `exam_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `time_range` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`exam_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `exam_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`creator_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `exam_question` (\n  `exam_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `question_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sequence_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`exam_id`, `question_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `exam_question_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`exam_id`) REFERENCES `exam` (`exam_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `exam_question_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`question_id`) REFERENCES `question` (`question_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_answer_sheet` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `exam_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `score` float NOT NULL,\n  `submission_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `exam_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_answer_sheet_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_answer_sheet_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`exam_id`) REFERENCES `exam` (`exam_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
